'''Chakna''' or '''chaakna''' is a spicy [[stew]], originating from the [[Indian subcontinent]], made out of [[tripe|goat tripe]] and other animal digestive parts. It is a speciality among [[Hyderabadi Muslim]]s. In all other parts of India, chakna refers to any snacks/finger foods for consumption with [[Alcoholic drink|alcohol]]. The tripe stew includes chunks of [[Liver (food)|liver]] and [[Kidney#As food|kidneys]].<ref>{{cite news |title= Biryani, Haleem & more on Hyderabad's menu|author= Sajjad Shahid|url= https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/hyderabad/Biryani-Haleem-more-on-Hyderabads-menu/articleshow/9617160.cms|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20121106044030/http://articles.timesofindia.indiatimes.com/2011-08-16/hyderabad/29891989_1_hyderabadi-cuisine-biryani-and-haleem-hyderabadi-dishes|url-status= live|archive-date= 6 November 2012|newspaper= [[The Times of India]]|access-date=3 February 2012}}</ref> It is usually taken with liquors throughout India.
